This package is an independent implementation of a bounded synthetic lesson.
The mechanism-aware one-bounce geometry is informed by arXiv:2605.01162v1.
It is not official author code, full GC-SAGE, or an experimental reproduction.

The simulator/evaluation contract follows the adjacent independently implemented
Python reference and the corrected all-channel-region lesson contract. Small
assignment ties follow SciPy 1.17's tested shortest-augmenting-path ordering;
SciPy is used only as an offline verification oracle, never imported at runtime.

The browser pseudorandom generator is explicitly versioned and differs from
NumPy PCG64. Tests use common arrays when comparing numerical solvers.

Do not publish offline truth/expected-output fixtures as live results or route
truth/evaluation metadata to the estimation worker.
